WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.836
Shapes.

2
00:00:00.996 --> 00:00:05.501
A shape is the outside edge of a thing, the line that goes all the way round it.

3
00:00:05.661 --> 00:00:07.007
A ball is a circle.

4
00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:08.561
A dice is a square.

5
00:00:08.721 --> 00:00:10.717
A slice of pizza is a triangle.

6
00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.364
A door is a rectangle.

7
00:00:12.524 --> 00:00:14.753
Once you start looking, shapes are everywhere.

8
00:00:15.453 --> 00:00:16.428
Patterns.

9
00:00:16.588 --> 00:00:19.189
A pattern says the same thing again and again.

10
00:00:19.349 --> 00:00:20.881
Red, blue, red, blue.

11
00:00:21.041 --> 00:00:22.759
Star, square, star, square.

12
00:00:22.919 --> 00:00:25.566
If you can say what comes next, it is a pattern.

13
00:00:25.726 --> 00:00:27.677
If it never repeats, it is not.

14
00:00:28.377 --> 00:00:29.817
Patterns in tiles.

15
00:00:29.977 --> 00:00:33.506
Tile makers cover a whole wall with the same shapes, repeated.

16
00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:38.496
A blue tile, a white tile, a blue tile, a white tile, and a star in every one.

17
00:00:38.656 --> 00:00:41.303
That is a pattern you can walk past every day.

18
00:00:42.003 --> 00:00:43.164
Making your own.

19
00:00:43.324 --> 00:00:47.782
You can make a pattern with anything: tiles, dots, zigzags, shapes.

20
00:00:47.942 --> 00:00:51.843
Choose two or three things, put them in a row, and say them again and again.

21
00:00:52.003 --> 00:00:54.464
That is your own pattern, and nobody else's.
